NeoModeration by Neomechanical filters Minecraft chat. It blocks swearing, slurs, scam links, ads for other servers and spam as soon as it is installed, with no account or API key.

[B]What a new install does[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Blocks messages that contain a word from starter lists of swear words and slurs: English, plus the Spanish, French, German, Portuguese or Turkish list that matches [FONT=Courier New]locale[/FONT] in [FONT=Courier New]config.yml[/FONT] ([FONT=Courier New]languagePacks[/FONT] turns on more). A word only matches from the start of a word to the end of one, so "assignment" and "Scunthorpe" stay clean, and everyday phrases that spell a banned word, such as "put a", are never read as it.
[*]Also matches common disguises of a listed word: spaced or stretched letters, accents, look-alike letters, leetspeak such as [FONT=Courier New]b4dw0rd[/FONT], and words split across rapid short messages.
[*]Blocks ads for other Minecraft servers: public IP addresses, addresses with a port, [FONT=Courier New]play.[/FONT] and [FONT=Courier New]mc.[/FONT] style addresses, free hosts such as [FONT=Courier New]aternos.me[/FONT], and "join myserver.net". Ordinary links stay. Let your own server's address through with [FONT=Courier New]/nmod allow url[/FONT].
[*]Blocks a starter list of IP-grabber and scam links, including ones written with [FONT=Courier New](dot)[/FONT] or [FONT=Courier New][.][/FONT].
[*]Blocks spam: message floods, the same message again and again and long runs of one character. Messages in capitals go out in lower case.
[*]Tells the player why a message was stopped, in their own game language.
[*]Alerts staff with the [FONT=Courier New]neomoderation.notify[/FONT] permission (operators by default), showing the player, the message, the reason and the action taken, with a clickable link to the player's case history.
[*]Lets moderators with [FONT=Courier New]neomoderation.moderate[/FONT] use cases, mutes and tests while settings stay with admins.
[*]Logs each detection as a case on your server. [FONT=Courier New]/nmod cases[/FONT] lists them; open one to resolve or dismiss it, allow the word or mute the player. The log leaves out the message text unless you turn it on.
[/LIST]
A new install never mutes, kicks or bans a player or clears chat. Review the starter lists for your server and change them with [FONT=Courier New]/nmod word[/FONT], [FONT=Courier New]/nmod url[/FONT] and [FONT=Courier New]/nmod allow[/FONT].

[B]First check[/B]
[LIST=1]
[*]Put the jar in [FONT=Courier New]plugins/[/FONT] and restart the server.
[*]Run [FONT=Courier New]/nmod test badword[/FONT]. The preview shows the starter rule flagging and blocking the word, and it never acts on a player.
[*]Run [FONT=Courier New]/nmod doctor[/FONT] to check your setup.
[/LIST]
To have local rules alert staff without blocking, run [FONT=Courier New]/nmod mode monitor[/FONT].

[B]Options, all off on a new install[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Star out matched words and links and let the rest of the message through ([FONT=Courier New]moderation.chat.censorLocalDetections[/FONT] in [FONT=Courier New]config.yml[/FONT]).
[*]Block every link and server IP address, including ones written with [FONT=Courier New](dot)[/FONT] or [FONT=Courier New][.][/FONT] ([FONT=Courier New]moderation.offline.blockAnyUrl[/FONT]).
[*]Check signs, books, anvil renames and chat commands such as [FONT=Courier New]/msg[/FONT] and [FONT=Courier New]/me[/FONT] with [FONT=Courier New]/nmod surface[/FONT]. Each can monitor, censor or block. Command checks also catch a player who sends those commands too fast.
[*]Send detection alerts to a Discord staff channel with [FONT=Courier New]/nmod discord[/FONT], and check the webhook with [FONT=Courier New]/nmod discord test[/FONT].
[*]Add actions after a block with [FONT=Courier New]/nmod action[/FONT]: clear chat, mute, kick or ban. Mutes need no other plugin and cover private messages too, and [FONT=Courier New]/nmod mute[/FONT] mutes a player by hand.
[*]Add a strike for each blocked or starred-out message and act when a player reaches a set count ([FONT=Courier New]moderation.strikes[/FONT]).
[/LIST]

[B]Optional cloud checks[/B]
The Neomechanical Moderation API can read each chat message for its meaning, in eight categories: sexual content, hate, harassment, violence, scams, spam, illicit activity and self-harm. It can also check map art when a player holds a filled map, puts one in an item frame or right-clicks one there.
[LIST]
[*][FONT=Courier New]/nmod trial[/FONT] explains what a free 14-day trial sends, and [FONT=Courier New]/nmod trial start[/FONT] starts it. It needs no account, and each server can start one trial.
[*]To use your own workspace, [URL='https://neomechanical.com/signup?src=neomoderation_spigot']create an account[/URL], create an API key with the [FONT=Courier New]events:write[/FONT] and [FONT=Courier New]usage:read[/FONT] scopes, and run [FONT=Courier New]/nmod setup <key>[/FONT].
[*]Cloud decisions only alert staff until you run [FONT=Courier New]/nmod cloudmode enforce[/FONT], and while they only alert, chat never waits for them. In enforce mode a flagged map is taken from the player holding it, and one hanging in an item frame is taken down.
[*][FONT=Courier New]/nmod preset family[/FONT], [FONT=Courier New]community[/FONT] or [FONT=Courier New]minimal[/FONT] sets how strict each category is.
[*]If the cloud cannot be reached, chat goes through and local rules keep running. Chat waits at most 2.5 seconds for a cloud answer.
[*]Each check sends one message, or one map image, with the player's name and UUID to [FONT=Courier New]api.neomechanical.com[/FONT] over HTTPS. Earlier messages are never sent. [FONT=Courier New]/nmod privacy[/FONT] shows what your settings send.
[*]Cloud checks use credits, and [FONT=Courier New]/nmod usage[/FONT] shows how many are left.
[/LIST]

[B]Privacy and metrics[/B]
Without an API key or a Discord webhook, no chat or map content leaves your server. NeoModeration sends technical metrics to bStats, which hold no chat, player names or API keys. Turn them off in [FONT=Courier New]plugins/bStats/config.yml[/FONT]. Once at startup, NeoModeration asks GitHub whether a newer version exists. Turn that off with [FONT=Courier New]updateCheck[/FONT] in [FONT=Courier New]config.yml[/FONT].

[B]Compatibility[/B]
NeoModeration runs on Bukkit, Spigot, Paper and Purpur, Minecraft 1.18.2 to 26.2. Release checks run on Paper 1.18.2, 1.19.4, 1.20.6 and 1.21.11. In-game messages are in English, Spanish, French, German, Portuguese or Turkish, and each player reads them in their own game language.

